// How to place this send in a timeline without downloading it, decided when it was sent from the
// `interaction.json` part it carried (no authentication check: the sending organization wrote it).
// Same values as on received email except that a send is never `pending`. Decided once by the server
// from the message's authoritative `interaction.json` part, and for received mail only when a
// passing DKIM signature covering From and Content-Type authenticates the From that wrote it; the
// `X-Primitive-Interaction` header is never used, so an unsigned or forged message is always `none`.
// `status`: a pure status signal (`read`, `working`, `typing`, or an `ack` that is the strict signal
// shape), to be shown as a property of the message it is about, not as a row. `card`: an interaction
// that renders as its own timeline item (`ack-request`, `wake.dispatch`, `primitive.contact`,
// `repeat.tick`, `repeat.stop`, and the reserved `approval` and `schedule.send`). `none`: ordinary
// mail, including any interaction kind not listed. Treat an unfamiliar value as `none`.
